decision: pass
reviewer: claude-opus-5-5 (self-review)
audience: Technical leads and maintainers
purpose: How do developers activate the standard, and which channel delivers it?

Records that activation is a single `install.sh` run with `engsys doctor` for diagnosis, and that origin/main is the release channel with the lock recording the checkout revision.
Translated from Korean to English; frontmatter including `superseded-in-part-by: 0023` is byte-identical, and commands, paths and ADR 0001/0002/0003 links are unchanged.
Headings mapped to Decision, Background and Constraints, Rationale and Alternatives, Consequences, in source order.
Source inconsistency kept as written: Decision says install.sh changes "one line" of the shell profile, Consequences says it adds "two lines"; not reconciled because this is a frozen record.
The marketplace rejection is translated as recorded in 2026-09-08 even though ADR 0023 later supersedes part of it. No Korean literals retained.

